  "question": {
    "text": "Sand is being dropped on a conveyer belt at the rate of $2 \\mathrm{~kg}$ per second. The force necessary to keep the belt moving with a constant speed of $3 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "v0XDl",
      "text": "\n$12 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DgZx8",
      "text": "\n$6 \\mathrm{~N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NzwwI",
      "text": "\nzero\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2p33D",
      "text": "\n$18 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, rate of fall of sand on conveyer belt,\n$$\n\\frac{d m}{d t}=2 \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\n$$\nConveyer belt speed $v=3 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$ Force $F=$ ?\n$$\nF=v \\frac{d m}{d t}=3 \\times 2=6 \\mathrm{~N}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
